  "title": "Spain Train Crash: A Deadly Collision Between Two Trains",
  "summary": "A deadly train collision between a high-speed train and another train on the same track in Spain resulted in at least 69 fatalities and 100+ injuries, with authorities investigating the cause. The incident, the second in less than a year on the same line, highlights growing concerns over infrastructure safety.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "A high-speed train from Madrid to Seville collided with another train on the same track, killing at least 69 people and injuring 100+.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both trains were brought to a halt earlier when the signalling system failed, with the driver of the state-owned Spanish train being told to restart the journey but crashing into the train in front.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The collision involved two trains on the same track, with the front carriages of the AVE train and the rear of the private operator's train being destroyed.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
